FFmpeg-based wasm decoder (decoder.js + decoder.wasm)

This is the buildable source of the decoder that ships with the Audio Player
extension. The prebuilt binaries live in v2/data/player/decoder/ and are a
drop-in replacement target for the artifacts produced here.

Derived from https://github.com/chandler-stimson/decoder.js (0.1.2) with the
following changes:

  * batch output is buffered (the original issued one fwrite per 4-byte
    sample, which dominated the decode time of large files)
  * an incremental streaming API (decoder_open / decoder_pull /
    decoder_seek / decoder_close) fed through JS callbacks so that playback
    can start before the whole file is downloaded and decoded
  * a use-after-free in the batch clean-up path was fixed

The batch entry point `decoder` keeps its 0.1.2 contract, so the binaries can
be swapped into the extension without any code change; the streaming API is
consumed by worker.js afterwards.

Build (requires emsdk, git, make, pkg-config):

  cd dev/decoder && bash build.sh

The output (decoder.js, decoder.wasm) is produced in this directory and must
replace the checked-in binaries in v2/data/player/decoder/.

A GitHub workflow (.github/workflows/build-decoder.yml) builds the artifacts
automatically on changes to this directory.
